WEBVTT

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.630
Hey, everybody, welcome to
Up To the Meme-ent!

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:07.910
I'm your host, Dani Fernandez.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.670
Nobody knows
who's making them,

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.190
but the whole world
is going bonkers...

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.870
over a series
of truly bizarre videos...

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.390
starring '80s-era bad guy
Wreck-It Ralph.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.510
Check out what
everyone is buzzing about...

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:19.750
over at BuzzzTube.com.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.590
Hey, guys,
Wreck-It Ralph here...

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.990
with the ghost pepper
challenge.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.030
Supposed to be spicy.
We'll see about that.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.030
Mmm. That's not so...

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.430
Oh, it's very hot!
Oh, make it stop!

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.310
(CHUCKLES) Yo, McNeely,
another one just dropped.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.390
Check it out, dude.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.350
Where are these things
coming from?

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:37.630
Hey, Josey, did you see
the pepper challenge?

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:38.710
JOSEY: Oh, not yet.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.150
I'm watching the one
where he just smacks his lips.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.310
It's disgusting.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:43.750
RALPH: You don't want
any real hard lines.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.390
You just want to blend that
out there, like this...

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.190
And that, my friends,

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:51.030
is how you achieve
the perfect cat eye.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.150
-(LAUGHTER)
-I always start

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.670
with the hootnanny.
Shift it into a floss.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:58.910
And now I finish with
a hot Marat. Huh? Huh?

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.310
Follow along with me,

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:04.110
and I'm gonna give this little
cloud a little friend...

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.070
-in the form of a tree.
-(LAUGHTER)

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:07.750
Everybody needs a friend.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:10.430
Look at these guys.

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:12.510
Look at this one,
sleeping under his ear.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:14.710
You couch potatoes.
Wake up.

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:17.750
We've been baking
at about 950 degrees

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:18.950
now for six hours...

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:20.750
so she should be ready.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:22.150
(COUGHING)

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.550
Voilà! Burnt pie!

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:26.390
Let's have a little whiff
of this here. (SNIFFS)

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.550
(SHOUTING) My hair, my hair!
My hair!

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:31.070
This man is on fire.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.350
Literal and figurative fire.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.310
But he still needs
200 million hearts

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:36.670
in the next five hours...

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.670
or this beautiful child
loses her game.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.150
That's why
I'm on to phase two...

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.670
you, my elite Pop-Up Army.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.790
I need you out there
popping up...

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.070
and getting clicks
all over the Internet.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:51.190
I'm talking Tumblr,
Instagram, Mashable.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.670
Be my pied pipers and

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.030
lead that beautiful traffic
to BuzzzTube...

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.830
because Wreck-It Ralph
needs his hearts.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:04.110
Hey, mister! Hey, yeah, yeah,
yeah, yeah, you, you.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.430
You don't wanna miss this.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:06.670
It's the latest
Wreck-It Ralph video.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.310
Click it. Click it!

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:23.550
Man oh Manischewitz,
that looks so fun.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:24.790
Yesss, can I be a pop-up?

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.430
I don't know. Can you be
annoyingly aggressive?

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:30.030
I don't know.
Can I? Can I? Can I?

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.630
Can I? Can I? Can I?
Can I? Can I? Can I?

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.710
Oh, yes, you're perfect. Here.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:36.990
Thank you!

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.190
If you're going, I wanna go.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:41.590
No, baby, you've got to stay
here and be my movie star.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.870
What? No, no, no. Me and the
kid are like shoes and socks.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:46.550
Or peanut butter and bacon.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:48.270
One cannot exist
without the other.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:49.510
Go on, kid, tell her.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:50.670
It's true.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.950
In fact, it's so true
that we will be fine

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.950
if we're apart for a minute.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.670
Come on, pal. It's my game
we're trying to save.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.390
I just wanna get out there
and be useful.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.070
But without me?

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:04.110
What if you get lost?
You're just a kid.

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:06.510
Oh, and you're
some mature adult?

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:08.510
Well, I'm bigger.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:10.430
Don't be insecure, big fella.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.710
She's not gonna get lost.
I promise.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.670
She'll be in
my personal web browser.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.910
And your app comes
with BuzzzFace...

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.350
so you can keep in touch
anywhere on the Internet.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.190
See, I'll be fine.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.230
I know, I just...

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:28.950
(SIGHS)

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:31.710
We haven't been apart
in like six years.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.750
I'm going to miss you.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:36.310
You'll be fine, too.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:38.350
The more hearts
your videos get,

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.070
the faster
we'll get the wheel.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.870
And then we can go home.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.270
Look, we'll be celebrating

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.630
at Tapper's this time
tomorrow, buddy.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:48.710
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:50.430
Bye!

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:53.710
Be careful, huh?
Don't be a dummy.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.310
(WHOOSHES)

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:56.710
(SIGHS)

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.350
So where exactly
are you sending her?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.790
Since candy girl
comes from an arcade game...

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.830
I'm thinking she'd be good
in the gaming district.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:06.870
Oh, no, no, no, no.
Bad idea.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:09.510
Those games are dangerous,
and they rot your brain.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:10.870
Why don't we
send her somewhere

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:13.470
a little more
totally different than that...

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:15.910
and nowhere near there?

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:18.950
Let's see.
Family Friendly Fansites.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.390
That sounds safe, and she is
technically a princess...

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:23.310
so how about this one here

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.070
with the sweet little
pink castle?

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.230
I love it.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:30.270
Okay, I'll redirect our newest
pop-up to OhMyDisney.com.

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:35.590
-(GIRLS CHEERING)
-(POP MUSIC PLAYING)

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:39.270
Jeez Louise, this place
is bonkers! Whoa!

